<div class="content-box" style="background: #fff3cd; border-left: 4px solid #ffc107;">
    <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb"></i> Watch Out For</h2>
    <p>Common misconceptions to avoid:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Private Variables in Python: Believing __variable is "secure" encryption rather than a naming convention (name mangling) meant to prevent conflicts.</li>
        <li>Static vs. Instance: Confusion over why changing a static variable affects all objects (e.g., changing a global interest rate vs. an individual account balance).</li>
    </ul>
